  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Integrated Humanitarian Assistance to the Most Vulnerable Crisis-Affected People through Mobile Teams in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Heavy clashes between the Rapid Support Forces and the Sudanese Armed Forces that erupted in on 15 April 2023 have already displaced more than 1 million people and affected the entire region. The unfolding crisis has resulted in a devastating humanitarian situation in and around countries bordering Sudan, creating additional needs to a situation that was already dire. Through this project, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is providing multi-sectoral humanitarian assistance in the form of health, nutrition, mental health and psychosocial support and protection to crisis-affected populations in three bordering states (Northern, White Nile and Gedaref) in Sudan. These integrated services are being provided by multi-disciplinary teams assisting the most vulnerable migrants, internally displaced persons (IDPs) and host community members. This multi-sectoral assistance contributes towards the improvement of the health, nutrition and protection environment faced by IDPs, migrants and host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
